  "raw_text": "147\n\nUpla yamnika dukiara lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto think about the well-being of others, to have empathy\n \n/ pensar en el\nbienestar de los demás, tener empatía\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-07/21\n):\n \nYawan upla yamnika dukiara luki ba marikisa taim, upla nani ba Jehova ra kakaira takaia want kabia\n\n–\n \nWhen we show that we are thinking about the well-being of others, people will want to come to know Jehovah\n \n/ Cuando\ndemostremos que estamos pensando en el bienestar de los demás, la gente querrá llegar a conocer a Jehová)\n\nUpla nahki ai dara wali ba ra lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto think about the well-being of others, to have empathy\n \n/ pensar en el\nbienestar de los demás, tener empatía\n\nUya lukras\n \n–\n \ndon’t care much\n \n/ no me importa mucho\n\nLukwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto boil, to bubble\n \n/ hervir, bullir, burbujear\n\nLula\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nknee, calf of the leg\n \n/ rodilla, pantorrilla\n\n(Construct:\n \nLuli\n \n–\n \nmy knee,\n \n... / mi rodilla, ...;\n \nLulam\n \n–\n \nyour knee, ...\n \n/ tu rodilla, ...\n;\n \nAi lula\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their knee, ...\n \n/ su rodilla, ...)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb38\n):\n \nAi lula nani purara yan Samson ba yapan\n \n–\n \nShe caused Samson to fall asleep on her lap\n \n/ Ella hizo que Sansón se\n\ndurmiera en su regazo\n)\n\nLula krikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto kneel\n \n/ arrodillarse\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb-60\n):\n \nNabucodonosor Daniel mawan ra ai lula kriki ai lal makupi bara win: ...\n \n–\n \nNebuchadnezzar kneeling down in\nfront of Daniel with his head facing downward said: ...\n \n/ Nabucodonosor se arrodilló frente a Daniel con la cabeza hacia\nabajo y dijo: ...)\n\nLulkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto throw, to toss, to throw away, to reject\n \n/ tirar, rechazar\n\nAi lulks\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \nThrow to me\n \n/ Tírame\n\nBîla\n \nlulkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto disobey\n \n/ desobedecer\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nLulkaia\n \nmeans\n \nto throw away\n, so this gives the idea of rejecting a command.\n \nIt\n \nis\n \na little different than\n \nBîla\n\nwalras\n \nwhich is simply\n \nnot obey\n \n/\n \nLulkaia\n \nsignifica\n \ntirar\n, así que esto da la idea de rechazar una orden. Es un poco\n\ndiferente a\n \nBîla walras\n, que simplemente\n \nno obedece\n)\n\nLat lulkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cast lots\n \n/ echar suertes\n\nLat lulki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cast lots to see who wins, to cast lots to see what the decision is\n \n/ echar suertes\npara ver quien gana, echar suertes para ver cuál es la decisión\n\nLulki aiks\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \nThrow to me\n \n/ Tírame\n\nLulki swiaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto abandon, to throw away, to leave behind\n \n/ abandonar, tirar, dejar atrás\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-17\n):\n \nBan kra witin nani ra lulki swiram baku ai dara walbia.\n \n–\n \nMaybe they will feel like you abandoned them.\n \n/\nQuizás sientan que los abandonaste.)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlrw-Matiu19:27\n):\n \nKais, yang nani diara sut lulki swisi man ninam blikri\n \n–\n \nLook, we have left all things behind and\nfollowed you\n \n/ Mira, hemos dejado todo atrás y te hemos seguido)\n\nMamna lulkaia\n \n(\ndb,dba,dbta,bh,sln,lrw,sn,mwb\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto groan, to sigh, to moan, to wail\n \n/ gemir, suspirar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-02/19\n):\n \nWan mamna lulki bîla sip aisaras kabia sin, nahki tnatka ra Jehova wan walisa?\n \n–\n \nIf we are not able to\nspeak our groanings (NWT-Romans 8:26-\n“unuttered groanings”), in what way does Jehovah listen to us?\n \n/ Si no podemos\nhablar nuestros gemidos (TNM-Romanos 8:26- \"lamentos no expresados\"), ¿de qué manera nos escucha Jehová?)\n\nMamna lulkanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngroaning, moaning, sighing, wailing\n \n/ gemir, suspirar\n\nSaki lulkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto take out and throw away, to remove and reject\n \n/ sacar y tirar, quitar y rechazar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-07/19\n):\n \nRug lâka lukanka taski kum sinski ra balisa kaka, isti saki lulkisna ki?\n \n–\n \nIf an immoral thought enters\nmy thinking, do I quickly throw it away?\n \n/ Si un pensamiento inmoral entra en mi mente, ¿lo descarto rápidamente?)\n\nTrisba lulkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto shoot with an arrow\n \n/ disparar con una flecha\n\nLupia\n \n–\n \ntiny, very small\n, mere\n \n/ pequeño, muy pequeño, mero\n \n(\nSee also/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nSirpi\n)\n\nLus tikaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nLus tiwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto lose\n \n/ perder\n\nLus tiwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nLus tikaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto lose\n \n/ perder\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh50\n):\n \nLus tiwan ba kli briaia dukiara...\n \n–\n \nIn order to have again what was lost...\n \n/ Para tener de nuevo lo que se perdió...)\n\nLus\n \n(v\n-\nimp form of\n \nLuaia\n \n/\n \nforma imperativa del verbo\n \nLuaia\n)\n \n–\n \npass\n \n/\n \npasa\n, pase, pasen\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nYu kum pain lus!\n \n–\n \nHave a good day!\n \n/ Pasa un buen día!\n)\n\nMâ\n \n(Ma)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npiece, mass, particle, fruit, seed,\n \ngrain,\n \nproduct\n \n/ pieza, masa, partícula, fruta, semilla,\n \ngrano,\n \nproducto\n\n(Construct:\n \nMâka,\n \n...\n)\n\nBarli\n \nm\nâ\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbarley grain\n \n/ grano de cebada\n\nBiara m\nâ\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfruit of the womb, any lump in the stomach\n \n/ fruto del vientre, cualquier bulto en el estómago\n\nDus mâ\n \n–\n \nfruit of the tree\n \n/ fruto del árbol\n\n(Construct:\n \nDusa mâ\n)\n\nKasau mâ\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncashew nut, cashew seed\n \n/ semilla de marañón",
